# Immaterial.ask -- Ableton Live theme XML, converted by tools/themes/ask_to_theme.py
# IMMATERIAL_MOD: Immaterial with ONE ROLE CHANGED, THE ACCENT
# (ViewCheckControlEnabledOn) D6B762 in place of Immaterial's pink FF91C3
# (architect 2026-11-05, session 56, his pick m1 of tmp/s56: a separate
# theme, `immaterial` unchanged -- "lowest overhead, most honest, and least
# churn if reversed"; THE SHADE 2026-11-06, session 62, his pick x2 of
# tmp/s62, "my eye was biased by the small diffs"; the `_mod` suffix marks a
# theme modified by hand or by rule, session 86, 2026-11-07).
#
# THE RECIPE: Immaterial's own SearchIndication ECCA6D, its muted gold,
# SHADED IN OKLCH (Bjorn Ottosson's matrices): its lightness set to L 78.8,
# the lightness of the FF91C3 it replaces, so the accent sits over the ground
# at the ~55 L Live gives Default and Immaterial alike; its hue kept (89.7);
# its chroma scaled by 78.8 / its own L; each linear channel clipped to
# [0, 1], sRGB-encoded, rounded half to even and clamped: D6B762. The plain
# ECCA6D read "too bright" (+61 L over the ground). The accent is the
# markers' chip and a lit key's face, and the lit press fill and the
# lit-but-inert face derive from it; every other role is Immaterial's, its
# ScaleAwareness (the radio keys' purple) among them. The shade was the app's
# own rule over Immaterial.ask 2026-11-05 .. 11-11 (src/gui/theme_ask.cpp,
# git history); since 2026-11-11, session 110, it is this file's one baked
# word.
